     "type": "text",
     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With apiToken, configSecret, kerberoast and tokenCache blocked, the attacker can still reach browserStore, appServer, ciRunner, dmzWeb, containerHost, iotDevice, memoryDump, workstation and codeRepo. Everything else that leads to the target is cut off. jumpHost and vpnSession need kerberoast. ssoLogin and dbLogin need tokenCache. rdpLogin needs configSecret. As a result localAdmin, domainAdmin, fileServer, monitoringHost, hypervisor, printServer, serviceAccount and secretsManager are all unreachable. That leaves no route to any parent of crownData:exfiltrate: vaultRead needs jumpHost or secretsManager, dbReplica needs hypervisor, printServer or serviceAccount, shareMount needs secretsManager, and mailArchive needs domainAdmin, printServer or fileServer. The target is not reachable.\"}\n```"
    }
